The error message Error: connect ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:52946 means that your request to 127.0.0.1 (localhost) on port 52946 was refused. This typically happens when:

The server you are trying to reach is not running on your local machine.
The server is running, but not listening on port 52946.
There is a firewall or security software blocking the connection.
The server crashed or was stopped after you started Postman.
How to troubleshoot:

Make sure the backend server or API you want to connect to is running on your machine.
Double-check that it is listening on port 52946.
Try opening 
http://127.0.0.1:52946
 in your browser to see if you get any response.
If you are running the server in a container (like Docker), ensure the port is mapped to your host.
If you recently changed the port, update the request URL in Postman.
